IV on the first day of renewed excavations at the Palace of Nestor, Pylos. 
Hundreds of artifacts of gold, silver, bronze, ivory, and semiprecious stones 
were found with the body of a single male, 30-35 years old, dubbed the “Griffin 
Warrior.” Many of the grave goods were manufactured in the Minoan world. Among 
the gold artifacts were four signet rings decorated with Minoan ritual scenes. 
