[AIMessage → tool] create_analysis({'text': 'For the purposes of a neutral 
encyclopedic article, the authenticity and provenance disputes surrounding the 
Ring of Nestor should be presented as an ongoing scholarly debate rather than 
resolved in favor of a single position. Early accounts by Evans and 
institutional narratives present the ring as a genuine Late Helladic gold signet
ring from a Mycenaean rock-cut tomb near Thisb\x13 in Boeotia, while later 
authors such as Hudler and Marinatos frame it as a problematic object, raising 
the possibility of a modern forgery and alternative find-spots such as Kakovatos
near Pylos. Pini\x19s technical study offers arguments for authenticity based on
manufacturing details. A balanced article will (1) describe Evans\x19s and 
museum accounts, (2) outline the later skepticism and proposed scenarios, and 
(3) make clear that no consensus has been reached, so the ring is often treated 
as a dubitandum in recent scholarship.', 'query_id': None})
